      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please fix this WARNING reported by autoreview issue finding: This condition changes the behavior of `ExpandModules` and breaks C++ module generation.\n\nThe original `ExpandModules` traversed through non-modules (targets where `module_type().none()` is true) to find the first layer of actual modules that need to be `extern`ed. This meant it would traverse through a `source_set`\u0027s `public_deps` if it didn\u0027t have a module map, in order to find the underlying modules.\nBy changing the traversal condition here to `target-\u003esources().empty() \u0026\u0026 target-\u003epublic_headers().empty()`, this will no longer traverse the `public_deps` of a `source_set` that has sources but no module map. Then `ExpandModules` will simply filter out this `source_set`, completely losing its transitive modules.\n\nAdditionally, for the layering check (`gn suggest`), stopping traversal at targets with sources is incorrect because `public_deps` are *always* forwarded to dependents in GN, regardless of whether the intermediate target has sources or not. If `B` has sources and `public_deps \u003d [C]`, depending on `B` gives you access to `C`\u0027s headers. But this function stops at `B` and won\u0027t find `C`, causing `Exposes(B, C)` to incorrectly return false.\n\nSince `ExpandModules` and `gn suggest` need different traversals (one skips non-modules, the other should traverse all `public_deps`), they shouldn\u0027t share this identical traversal logic unless it is parameterized.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 88,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 88,
        "endChar": 0
      },
